{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point of hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> (or its extension) of isosceles right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822d619e1e23af0c9ee5e0e90038b35ef2e1bcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=AP^2+PB^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />. Then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d67cc557a87462d7c779bec657825d963c267ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } s&lt;2CP^2 \\text{ for a finite number of positions of P}\\quad\\\\ \\text{(B) } s&lt;2CP^2 \\text{ for an infinite number of positions of P}\\quad\\\\ \\text{(C) } s=2CP^2 \\text{ only if P is the midpoint or an endpoint of AB}\\quad\\\\ \\text{(D) } s=2CP^2 \\text{ always}\\quad\\\\ \\text{(E) } s&gt;2CP^2 \\text{ if P is a trisection point of AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1748be8fdda4aab8b3336f294ee58fe979632d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,50),B=(50,0),C=(0,0); draw(A--B--C--A); dot(A); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NE); dot(B); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); dot(C); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW);  pair P=(14,36); dot(P); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,NE); draw((0,36)--P,dotted); draw((14,0)--P,dotted);  label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(7,36),S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(0,43),W); label(&quot;$x-a$&quot;,(14,18),E); label(&quot;$x-a$&quot;,(32,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</p><p>Consider the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the hypotenuse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  Draw perpendicular lines from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> towards the sides.  Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd2863f2ee194e8caddfd9acc5cd516a94cb783.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP^2 = a^2 + a^2\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be96a88f3da8160a0422413fe7186fc43e4aea5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BP^2 = (x-a)^2 + (x-a)^2\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fb0538976aa1db46739e57b0f2e4807b8a020f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CP^2 = a^2 + (x-a)^2\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" />\nThis means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995cb2e37316eda1ee190b770bddd1e7d6c76eb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = 4a^2 - 4ax + 2x^2\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be06805db45c49ce66a61a31e833af6e3d871ce3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\cdot CP^2 = 4a^2 - 4ax + 2x^2\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1effe316b9d5446c74816a405a2648f3ecfdbc1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 2 \\cdot CP^2$\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the hypotenuse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f95d7e387f75cd5154f434f24e3e868e0d92a17a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,50),B=(50,0),C=(0,0); draw(A--B--C--A); dot(A); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NE); dot(B); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); dot(C); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW);  pair P=(-10,60); dot(P); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,NE); draw(P--A); draw(P--(-10,50)--A,dotted); draw(P--(-10,0)--C,dotted);  pair D=(-10,50); dot(D); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW);  label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(-10,55),W); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(-5,50),S); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(0,25),E); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(25,0),S);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" />\n</p><p>Consider the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be between point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and draw perpendicular line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Also, draw point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7c0e2699de5e9e32a5ec920d91b723da4dd634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD \\parallel AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba1b4e3c1d6fb68bba7123d42a88cd81b245ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA \\parallel CB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Using the Pythagorean Theorem again,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd2863f2ee194e8caddfd9acc5cd516a94cb783.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP^2 = a^2 + a^2\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e079d3352b67eb2c2974e85ed8a7456ac02ece.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BP^2 = (a+x)^2 + (a+x)^2\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c19ed297ed217d0212f4ac18a2fc2d2cd635bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CP^2 = (a+x)^2 + a^2\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\nThat means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b116d1cb6250cb65ef38d51a5ba6db6084d7a7ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = 4a^2 + 4ax + 2x^2\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fea36b4b94d7c151716eb098ebcca505df1ab5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\cdot CP^2 = 4a^2 + 4ax + 2x^2\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1effe316b9d5446c74816a405a2648f3ecfdbc1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 2 \\cdot CP^2$\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the hypotenuse.\n</p><p>In summary, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e845e9547e97d2a76d27346ceba63e1b1c0d977c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2 + BP^2 = 2 \\cdot CP^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit sectio